rsal, and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste distributes matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeats the whole text. Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal handling, metadata invalidation, and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL and thin primary/secondary carets: vertical bars where supported, underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture pipeline, recovered source/documentation, diagnostic evidence, and authenticated task history. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering. All execution occurs on GitHub.\n\n- Run cursor-history regressions first: repeated indent/undo/replacement, abandoned redo branches replaced by indentation, unindentation or editing, checkpoint eviction, document reset, explicit history clearing, inherited edits, and no-op preservation.\n- Assert observable text and cursor restoration alongside bounded metadata retention. Retain reversed selections and independent preferred-column checks.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Preserve branch **98.03%**, combined **98.92%**, statement **99.22%**, and all subsystem floors.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route for all 46 scenes. Bind capture evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies, and base. Independently inspect every full PNG and geometry result before correction publication; retain comparison evidence and explicit incomplete results.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review, then complete independent implementation review covering every diff continuation, diagnostic helper/test, capture/scene change, and companion implementation. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must complete and safely activate the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Record questions with resolver decisions; recommendations do not substitute for protected approval.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. Completing this bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ee81771267af8eec15d44668ff4aa88017da5dbfadea162fa68e370175ffd805","text":"# Correct PR #9 document resets and CI fixtures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `b346d04a90b5edc073a4c384eae98e3150b883f0`, against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies stale secondary cursors after document replacement and two test-fixture failures. The independent resolver selected **Reset state**. No material question remains; this selection supplies no implementation, visual, merge, or protected-policy approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, extend `load_text()` to clear secondary selections, old preferred-column mappings, and cursor-history snapshots **before** calling Textual’s implementation. Preserve Textual’s primary-cursor reset behavior and the existing method signature. Use only state initialized before `super().__init__()`; avoid mount-dependent selection helpers during construction.\n- Preserve shared history recording/pruning for edits and indentation, exact live-edit identity tracking, undo/redo restoration, inherited-edit maintenance, and no-op redo preservation. Keep idle pruning active.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, construct the eviction-test history with all required arguments: `max_checkpoints=2`, `checkpoint_timer=60.0`, and `checkpoint_max_characters=1000`. Retain explicit transaction checkpoints and every eviction, metadata-bound, text, selection, and preferred-column assertion.\n- Extend its parameterized reset regression for both `load_text()` and the `text` setter. Create mounted cursors and reversed selections across several rows with distinct preferred columns, populate undo and redo, then replace with shorter single-line text and empty text.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/completion_readiness.py`, complete the idle fixture with empty undo/redo stacks, cursor-history metadata, and a callback invoking the real pruning method. Retain assertions that idle reopens retained suggestions and leaves dismissed suggestions closed.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support, protected workflows, and diagnostic interfaces remain unchanged.\n\n## Required behavior retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection preserves independent preferred columns through reversal, short lines, and boundaries without creating cursors.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing supports multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste use matching fragments, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, vertical bars where supported and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. The inspected published-head picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Run the two failing modules first on canonical Python 3.11, Python 3.8 minimum dependencies, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest dependencies.\n- Reset regressions must assert one valid primary cursor, no secondary cursors or obsolete preferences, cleared history/snapshots, safe rendering after layout settles, and typing at only the reset cursor. Undo/redo must not resurrect the old document or cursors. Retain construction and unmounted-reset coverage.\n- Run existing history lifecycle, multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head static/lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Obtain canonical coverage JSON; retain **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed coverage test run establishes no new ratchet shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate on GitHub and independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication. Bind evidence to the actual source, candidate, checkpoint, base, task, plan, and dependencies; published-head captures do not validate new edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete implementation review afterward, including every diff continuation and the RPi companion implementation. Earlier incomplete reviews supply no approval.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of recommendation-policy companion work and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices, retaining question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not replace that overall completion requirement.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a07d171e6d4a09c77a547e9facb213584f0e78ae82abcdb5c2ab3d0a7c6c4974","text":"# Correct PR #9’s unmounted-reset test context\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `a30ce3df206677c416b34e06b99e97e80764d1f1` against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies four failures in the unmounted-reset regression. Python 3.8/3.9 lack an event loop; Python 3.10–3.12 lack an active Textual app. The independent resolver selected **Active app context**. No material question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, wrap the existing parameterized unmounted-reset test body in an asynchronous exercise invoked through `asyncio.run()`. Construct `SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession())` and enter `app.run_test()` before constructing either detached editor.\n- Keep both editors outside the mounted widget tree. Explicitly assert that each remains unmounted after construction and relevant operations.\n- Preserve all four parameter combinations, construction checks, no-op undo/redo checks, reset assertions, cursor/preferences cleanup, and empty history/snapshot assertions.\n- Retain the mounted reset/render/type regressions and shared history lifecycle unchanged. Do not catch or suppress Textual lifecycle errors, skip environments, or weaken assertions.\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered source/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Fully read edited files before writing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n- Public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic interfaces, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste: matching fragments first, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending second, otherwise whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled captures, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Inspected published-head PNGs supply no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run all four corrected cases and the complete cursor-history module on GitHub: Python 3.8 minimum/latest, canonical Python 3.11, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest. Require explicit unmounted-state assertions to pass.\n- Run adjacent lifecycle and completion-readiness tests, then focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/selection, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle coverage.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Obtain fresh canonical coverage JSON. Preserve **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate through the trusted GitHub route. Independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication, retaining picker comparisons. Bind evidence to actual source, candidate, checkpoint, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward. Review every diff continuation, including previously unfinished diagnostic/capture modules, associated tests, and immutable companion implementation and exact-commit CI evidence. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of the RPi recommendation-policy work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This test correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","questions":[{"answer_index":16,"id":"fbd480038ee660edb95dd3690683161a39480ffc41dfac01f8e147887794ef84","text":"Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export."},{"answer_index":18,"id":"9a11147e3ffd85ce140c8f1244a1b15377efd00916e606a8b431a2d03a92488d","text":"The fresh receipt binds capture `38731476440` to candidate `3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5` and the saved checkpoint. Widget rows, compositor rows and parsed SVG all retain the complete heading, including the `c`. This does not establish a production picker defect.\n\n1. **Coordinator tooling question:** Can `read_evidence_image` be exposed in this planner session for the supplied hash-bound PNG? It is absent from the available tools, and `read_image` returns “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” PNG inspection is still needed before specifying a presentation or export correction.\n\nNo owner decision or replacement upload is needed. Raw SVG bytes are not supplied. The publication transport repair also remains coordinator-owned; complete task history must be preserved."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"16d4d781180edfb004dda9a37d5c640ea072ea2cc5775a4681e92c27f584ab07","text":"Can the coordinator provide the reviewed plan’s GitHub reproduction with actual raw and framed SVG bytes, renderer versions, and available/selected font diagnostics, bound to the candidate, checkpoint and PNG hashes? PNG inspection now works and confirms the obscured `c`; terminal rows and parsed SVG preserve it. The supplied artifacts still cannot distinguish framing from rasterization, so a correction would be speculative."},{"answer_index":20,"id":"9d7dfd33ccfb0fff403dc64cf5154bb0084c6d340b3db71751df45304dbb3650","text":"Coordinator: please expose the exact pre-invocation checkpoint source for tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py. I mistakenly treated a capped 300-line read as complete and omitted its remaining lines when writing. Restore that file’s original suffix before retaining my focused additions. Please also verify the restored README against the saved checkpoint. No owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":21,"id":"962ad2658075e133178b0c27a43c436c00ea5a63640a4a6e0dafbca91a41dc09","text":"Coordinator: please run the approved isolated GitHub candidate capture from the preserved checkpoint, including the restored diagnostic tests and existing SVG-evidence helper/tests. Expose hash-bound database-picker raw/framed SVG content, font/renderer diagnostics and PNG through source_files. The reviewed plan requires this evidence before selecting a heading correction; no owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":22,"id":"d82141d33b770fcc68e14949f0292959e0f2597aa4301b71d32ab7338f57b0e7","text":"1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together."},{"answer_index":23,"id":"e896f2e46da935a3d8d2023d77a872fd7f6624fbdae4625988d391767b3be2a6","text":"I read the complete current-head check records and all failed-job log parts. Existing feature requirements remain settled; no new owner preference is needed. Three coordinator evidence questions remain before a concrete repair plan:\n\n1. **Picker correction:** Can the coordinator expose capture `38927473247`’s hash-bound receipt, database-picker geometry, complete raw/framed SVGs, and all four comparison PNGs? The visual evidence tools currently return “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” The reviewer’s framing finding needs direct inspection before selecting the export correction.\n\n2. **Coverage:** Can the coordinator expose canonical `coverage.json` from run `38927048857`, bound to head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2`? Branch coverage is **98.02% against 98.03%**. Exact missing arcs are needed to specify meaningful task-related regressions without changing baselines.\n\n3. **Type-menu failure:** Can the coordinator provide a bounded GitHub reproduction capturing focus, `type_input`, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry, and queued layout state immediately before the failing initial `assert menu.display` on Python 3.13/3.14? This will distinguish fixture timing from a production positioning defect before choosing a repair.\n\nThese are coordinator artifact requests, not requests for owner uploads or approval. No files were changed and no programs were executed."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"sql explorer: 1) if ctrl+shift+arrow up/down is pressed, then we should not spawn multiple cursors, instead selection should be expanded to the left until the line start, and next line until cursor's column (vs code like), it can be repeated multiple times to select many lines 2) now it seems that when multiple cursors is spawned, then I ctrl+c something and ctrl+v each cursor inserts WHOLE clipboard. instead each should have its own clipboard (VS code like)","task_id":"e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","version":2}